    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds **ADR-035: Layout-Integrated `<img>`** — resolves two of ADR-034's four honest limitations: below-fold thumbnails no longer overlap text, and the tagline unhides cleanly.\n\n**Documentation only.** Implementation lands in a follow-up PR.\n\n## The two problems this fixes\n\nADR-034 shipped `<img>` paint at paint time. Images render (PNG via Cairo, SVG via librsvg) but **don't reserve layout space** — the box stays at its zero-height intrinsic from layout, and paint draws over whatever's underneath.\n\nVisual consequence:\n- **Wordmark renders, tagline overlaps it** — hidden as a paint-layer workaround\n- **Below-fold thumbnails render, text below them is overlapped** — Tim Berners-Lee photo, HTML5 logo, categories diagram all obscure what comes after\n\n## Measurement (viewport 1774, Wikipedia HTML)\n\n### Baseline timing\n\n**5.03–5.48 sec** per render (3-run sample). That's the cost of a Wikipedia render today with no layout-time fetches.\n\n### All `<img>` boxes in tree (all `h=0`)\n\n| Element | Position | w | h |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Wordmark | 52, 14 | 248 | **0** |\n| Tagline | 52, 19 | 248 | **0** |\n| TBL photo | 324, 1253 | 926 | **0** |\n| HTML5 logo | 346, 6437 | 926 | **0** |\n| Categories diagram | 346, 14881 | 926 | **0** |\n| Login pixel | 324, 61935 | 948 | **0** |\n| Footer wikimedia | 67, 62163 | 1646 | **0** |\n| Footer mediawiki | 67, 62163 | 1646 | **0** |\n\n### Header is auto-height (not fixed)\n\n```css\n.mw-header {\n    display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center;\n    padding: 8px 0; gap: 16px;\n    min-height: 3.125rem;  /* 50px min, grows with content */\n}\n```\n\n**Can grow.** Tagline unhides cleanly; header expands to fit both wordmark (39px) + tagline (19px) ≈ 58px + padding = ~74px.\n\n## The decision\n\n`ImageDimLookup` callback threaded through `layout()` as a 5th parameter, defaulted to `nullptr`. Mirrors the `TextMeasurer` pattern from ADR-011.\n\n```cpp\nstruct ImageDim {\n    float width = 0.0f;\n    float height = 0.0f;\n    bool valid = false;\n};\nusing ImageDimLookup = std::function<ImageDim(const std::string&)>;\n\nLayoutBox layout(const dom::Document& doc,\n                 const css::ComputedStyleMap& styles,\n                 TextMeasurer measurer,\n                 float viewport_width,\n                 ImageDimLookup image_dims = nullptr);\n```\n\n**Default `nullptr` means zero existing test changes.** All 425 existing tests keep passing unmodified.\n\n### In `layout_element`, when `el.tag() == \"img\"`:\n\n1. **Explicit CSS width set** → use it, aspect-derive height\n2. **Explicit CSS height set** → use it, aspect-derive width\n3. **Neither** → use intrinsic dims directly (CSS-spec behavior)\n4. **Callback null or invalid** → existing behavior (h=0)\n\n### `RenderPipeline::relayout()` wires the callback:\n\n```cpp\nlayout_root_ = renderer::layout::layout(\n    *doc_, styles_cache_, &measure_with_pango, viewport_width,\n    [this](const std::string& url) -> renderer::layout::ImageDim {\n        cairo_surface_t* s = get_image_surface(url);\n        if (!s) return {};\n        return {\n            static_cast<float>(cairo_image_surface_get_width(s)),\n            static_cast<float>(cairo_image_surface_get_height(s)),\n            true\n        };\n    });\n```\n\n**Cache hit = zero cost.** First render: 8 sync fetches (5.0 → 5.4-5.8s). Subsequent layouts hit cache.\n\n## Expected visible delta\n\n| Check | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Wordmark | 248×0 | **248×39** |\n| Tagline | hidden | **248×19 (visible)** |\n| Header height | ~50 | **~74** |\n| Intro y | 145 | **~169** |\n| TBL photo | 926×0 | **926×~695** |\n| HTML5 logo | 926×0 | **926×~695** |\n| Categories | 926×0 | **926×~695** |\n| Text below thumbnails | overlapped | **starts below** |\n\nPNG will **differ** from ADR-034's baseline — that's the delta.\n\n## Four honest caveats\n\n1. **First-render-slow** — 5.0 sec → 5.4-5.8 sec cold cache (10%). Cached after. Real cost of sync-fetch at layout; documented as \"first-render-slow, subsequent-fast\" (same as any browser's first paint).\n2. **Footer SVGs use intrinsic dims** (50×50, 25×25) when no explicit CSS width set. Wikipedia's footer has `width:100%` so this branch isn't hit for the current page — but matters for future. ADR-036 (`max-width` support) refines.\n3. **Article content shifts 24px down** — correct behavior (header grows).\n4. **Search icon still 2×2** — needs `calc()`, separate ADR.\n\n## Design decisions\n\n### Callback vs. pre-pass\n\n`ImageDimLookup` mirrors the `TextMeasurer` pattern (consistency). Lazy (no fetch if display:none culls). Streaming (single pass, no double-walk). Testable (stub callback → hermetic tests).\n\nA pre-pass walking the tree to fetch all `<img>` before layout would work too, but: doubles outer walk cost, eagerly fetches display:none images, breaks the TextMeasurer precedent.\n\n### Default `nullptr`\n\nZero test churn for 425 existing tests. New tests explicitly pass stubs. Old behavior preserved unmodified.\n\n### Why not `object-fit`\n\n`object-fit: contain` (letterbox), `cover` (crop), `fill` (stretch) — none used on current Wikipedia assets. Deferred to ADR-036+.\n\n### Footer SVG resolution\n\nThe two footer `<img>` have `width: 100%; height: auto` inside a `max-width`-bounded container. Without `max-width` support, they'd be 1646×1646 (square) at 100% width. **v1 falls back to intrinsic dims when no explicit CSS width is set** — footer SVGs (50×50, 25×25) render at that intrinsic size. Matches CSS spec fallback (intrinsic when no explicit width).\n\n## What's next\n\nAfter ADR-035, remaining honest limitations:\n- **`calc()` evaluation** — search icon (2×2 today), needed for correct icon sizing\n- **`max-width` property** — footer SVGs, other width-constrained containers\n- **JPEG decode** — thumbnails need `libjpeg-turbo`\n- **`object-fit`** — non-intrinsic aspect handling\n\nEach own ADR. ADR-035 clears the biggest visible delta remaining after ADR-034.\n\nRefs #184\n",
